, dietary patterns, and cardiovascular risk"}]}, {"id": "8dcf39aa-9059-47cb-a939-9bae5dc766e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Renal, GI, and liver conditions", "description": "This subtopic shows how disease states change nutrient needs and restrictions.", "children": [{"id": "b98d2b9a-32f1-41f2-bfe6-a04fc78fc34f", "type": "concept", "title": "CKD, dialysis, sodium, potassium, phosphorus, protein, and fluids"}, {"id": "fb73e787-14ec-424a-b2ba-150cb2605e9a", "type": "concept", "title": "GERD, IBD, IBS, celiac disease, and malabsorption"}, {"id": "a057964b-4334-4d9e-9afb-745ac42fcec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Liver disease, ascites, and protein-energy needs"}]}, {"id": "6f536b2f-66f8-44d8-aabf-ea965a018ad8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Chronic care and patient education", "description": "Students learn to translate medical nutrition therapy into realistic patient plans.", "children": [{"id": "e4e7e911-452a-43ad-8dee-1f987ef64682", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-management and behavior change"}, {"id": "00d68f1c-c61e-4486-abd0-e57f388b8d3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Food access, culture, cooking skills, and family systems"}, {"id": "a51e85e5-fb0e-417e-818a-5b3c51b6711d", "type": "concept", "title": "Monitoring, follow-up, and referral"}]}]}, {"id": "90103e44-4e6f-4e52-ad83-42463e99fc04", "type": "topic", "title": "Therapeutic diets, enteral/parenteral nutrition, and complex clinical nutrition", "description": "Introduce nutrition support, malnutrition, refeeding risk, wounds, surgery, oncology, and acute care nutrition.", "children": [{"id": "60de90d2-1922-49db-ac1b-d982de3b5ef1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Therapeutic diets and modified textures", "description": "Students learn common diet orders and why they are used.", "children": [{"id": "9b2b0632-8285-41d6-9397-5ecebabf2b8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistent carbohydrate, cardiac, renal, low sodium, high protein, and allergy diets"}, {"id": "bd676f1d-3a5e-4853-b0a5-e676a97942fb", "type": "c